---
/**
 * /about/, and who is writing all this.
 *
 * A prose page with two designed moments: the portrait, treated so it belongs on
 * a near-black ground rather than sitting on it as a light rectangle, and the
 * Pragmatic Programmer line, which was buried mid-paragraph and uncited on the
 * Jekyll page and is now a display pull quote with a visible attribution.
 *
 * The copy has been through the ticket 08 editorial pass. The degree is a return:
 * the gap is gestured at and never explained, and nothing here frames any of it as
 * a career change. No em-dashes: the gate fails the build on one.
 */
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageTitle from '../components/PageTitle.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import portrait from '../assets/img/dustin-jones.jpg';

// Titles and dates only. The case studies are the descriptions, so none are
// repeated here. Ranges use "to": the gate fails on a dash.
//
// The first entry deliberately does NOT match the resume, which names the
// employer. The employer is not named anywhere on this site (2026-09-17). The
// resume PDF in public/ is the one deliberate exception. Do not "fix" this.
const experience = [
  { org: 'A clinical CRO, Pennsylvania', role: 'Software Engineering Intern', when: 'Jun to Aug 2026' },
  { org: 'MSU Denver Honors Program', role: 'Student Assistant', when: 'Jan 2026 to present' },
  { org: 'Ember Capital Partners, Denver', role: 'Software Engineering Intern', when: 'Nov 2025 to Mar 2026' },
  { org: 'Vail Resorts, Colorado and Australia', role: 'Ski Instructor', when: '2020 to 2025' },
  { org: 'MSU Denver', role: 'B.S. Computer Science, Mathematics minor', when: 'Expected Dec 2027' },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Software engineer in Denver, finishing a B.S. in Computer Science at MSU Denver. Five seasons teaching skiing before this, and a quoting system modelled on an office."
>
  <PageTitle label={`${site.role}, ${site.location}`} lines={['About']} />

  <section class="grid gap-10 border-t border-line px-(--gutter) pb-16 pt-10 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-14">
    {/* At lg the portrait is five of twelve columns AND runs off the left edge of
        the page, out through the gutter. Four columns inside the gutter left it a
        modest rectangle with empty ground on three sides; at this size and this
        position it is the thing the page opens with rather than an illustration
        beside the opening. The slot is still a fraction of the grid, not a fixed
        width, so it keeps growing past 1440, and `sizes` describes that.

        The candidates stop at 1000 because that is the source file's own width.
        At the old four-column size the largest one was comfortably above what a
        2x screen asked for. At 42vw a 2x 1440 screen wants about 1220 and can
        only be handed the 1000, so it upscales by a fifth. Listing a 1280 or a
        1600 does not fix that, it just emits candidates the pipeline clamps back
        to 1000; a larger export of the portrait would, and the original lives on
        the career-hub side. */}
    <div
      class="portrait max-w-[18rem] lg:col-span-5 lg:-ml-(--gutter) lg:max-w-none"
    >
      <Image
        src={portrait}
        alt="Dustin Jones"
        widths={[320, 480, 640, 960, 1000]}
        sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 42vw, 18rem"
        loading="eager"
      />
    </div>

    {/* Not a [data-reveal]: it is the first thing anyone reads on the page and
        it sits inside the first screenful.
        `self-end` lands it on the portrait's foot. Aligned to the top it stopped
        a third of the way down and left a tall empty block beside the rest of
        the photograph; at the foot the two blocks finish together and the space
        that is left is above the paragraph, where the heading already is. */}
    <p
      class="font-display text-3xl font-medium leading-[1.15] text-ink lg:col-span-6 lg:col-start-7 lg:self-end"
    >
      I'm a software engineer in Denver, finishing a B.S. in Computer Science at MSU Denver with a
      4.0 GPA and a minor in mathematics, graduating December 2027. I started this degree years
      ago, stopped, and came back to it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <div class="xl:grid xl:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_16rem] xl:gap-x-8 xl:pr-(--gutter)">
  <div class="prose pb-24">
    <p>
      In between I taught skiing professionally for Vail Resorts for five seasons, in Colorado and
      in Australia.
    </p>

    <p>
      Ski school runs on requests, priority lists, and who is visible to the people handing out
      work. That is the model the quoting system was built on: who got
      to see what, how a task arrived on someone's screen, what people did and did not know about
      each other's work. Its six roles are a model of the organization more than they are a
      security feature.
    </p>

    {/* Deliberately not "the shift", "the switch" or anything else that reads as a
        career change. The observation is about whose work is visible, and the
        page never explains the gap in the degree. */}
    <p>Skiing was legible to anyone watching. Programming is not.</p>

    {/* A sourced claim, so it is marked up as one: a blockquote with a cite URL
        and a visible attribution. The wording is verbatim and the attribution is
        to Ward Cunningham, who wrote the foreword; it is not Hunt and Thomas's
        line, and the cite points at the foreword itself rather than at the
        publisher's page for the book. */}
    <figure class="pullquote" data-reveal>
      <blockquote cite="https://c2.com/doc/pragmatic.html">
        <p>Most programmers would have trouble explaining what they do.</p>
      </blockquote>
      <figcaption>
        Ward Cunningham, foreword to <cite>The Pragmatic Programmer</cite>
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <p>
      That is the adjustment. The case studies here are the attempt at an explanation.
    </p>

  </div>

  {/* The second lane. A case study keeps its chapters here; this page has one
      section and keeps its availability instead, sticky beside the prose from
      xl and in flow under it below that. The line appears once on the page. */}
  <aside class="border-t border-line px-(--gutter) py-10 xl:sticky xl:top-24 xl:self-start xl:border-0 xl:px-0 xl:pt-2">
    <p class="label">Availability</p>
    <p class="mt-5 max-w-56 text-base leading-snug text-ink">
      Open to part-time and contract work, Denver or remote.
    </p>
    <ul class="mt-6 space-y-2">
      <li><a class="label transition-colors hover:text-accent" href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a></li>
      <li><a class="label transition-colors hover:text-accent" href={site.resume}>Resume, PDF</a></li>
      <li><a class="label transition-colors hover:text-accent" href={site.github}>GitHub</a></li>
      <li><a class="label transition-colors hover:text-accent" href={site.linkedin}>LinkedIn</a></li>
    </ul>
  </aside>
  </div>

  <section class="border-t border-line px-(--gutter) py-16">
    <h2 class="label">Experience</h2>
    <dl class="experience mt-8">
      {
        experience.map((e) => (
          <div>
            <dt>{e.org}</dt>
            <dd>
              <span>{e.role}</span>
              <span class="label">{e.when}</span>
            </dd>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="border-t border-line px-(--gutter) py-16">
    <p class="label">Read next</p>
    <a href="/process/" class="group mt-6 flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-8 gap-y-2">
      <span
        class="font-display text-[clamp(2rem,9vw,5.5rem)] font-extrabold uppercase leading-none tracking-tight text-ink transition-colors duration-300 group-hover:text-accent"
        >How I work</span
      >
      <span class="label transition-colors group-hover:text-accent">Process</span>
    </a>
    <div class="mt-12 flex flex-wrap gap-6 border-t border-line pt-6">
      <a class="label transition-colors hover:text-accent" href="/">All work</a>
      <a class="label transition-colors hover:text-accent" href={site.github}>GitHub</a>
      <a class="label transition-colors hover:text-accent" href={site.linkedin}>LinkedIn</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<script>
  import { withMotion, revealDisplayTitle, revealOnScroll } from '../scripts/motion';

  withMotion(() => {
    revealDisplayTitle();
    // The pull quote only. Body copy is painted before anything scroll-triggered
    // runs, because this page exists to be read.
    revealOnScroll('[data-reveal]');
  });
</script>
